  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Boil the kettle.\n• Cut falafel into quarters. In a large frying pan, heat a drizzle of olive oil (1/4 cup for 2P / 1/2 cup for 4P) over medium-high heat.\n• Cook the falafel until golden, 5-6 mins. Transfer to a paper towel-lined plate. Cover to keep warm.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/61c41349b18e00052a322f7a/step-c5524c1b.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Finely chop or crush garlic.\n• In a medium saucepan, melt butter (for the couscous) over medium-high heat. Cook garlic stirring, until softened, 1-2 mins.\n• Add the water (for the couscous) and chicken stock and bring to the boil.\n• Stir in couscous and a drizzle of olive oil. Cover and remove from heat. Set aside until water is absorbed, 5 mins.\n• Roughly chop parsley. Add to the couscous and toss to combine. Season to taste.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/61c41349b18e00052a322f7a/step-90def707.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Finely chop brown onion. Finely chop or crush garlic.\n• Wipe and return frying pan to medium-high heat with a drizzle of olive oil. Cook onion until softened, 4-5 mins.\n• Add garlic seasoning and tomato paste and cook until fragrant, 1 min.\n• Stir in the water (for the sauce) and the butter and cook until bubbling, 1-2 mins. Season to taste.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/61c41349b18e00052a322f7a/step-bf37417e.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Chop tomato and cucumber.\n• In a medium bowl, combine tomato and cucumber and a drizzle of white wine vinegar and olive oil. Season to taste.\n• Divide the couscous, falafel and salsa between bowls. Spoon the rich tomato sauce over the falafel.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/61c41349b18e00052a322f7a/step-c90e1e27.jpg"
    }
  ]
